      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the usual maximum.\n\n- **Maximum daily dose:** The label maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Some guidelines allow up to 2,000\u20133,000 mg/day. Extended-release is capped at 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n- **Maximum single dose:** A single dose is usually no more than 850\u20131,000 mg. A 1,700 mg dose would also raise the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis.\n\nCould this be a typo? Here are some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** That's 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg total per day.** This could be 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals.** That's 2,000 mg/day.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and whether it's immediate-release or extended-release. I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that, and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose."
      }
     ],
